    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴ</span></b> , exclam. of pain, grief, pity,
		astonishment, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ah! woe!</i>
			sts. with nom., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἲ᾽ γώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					803
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				674
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1115
			</span></i> : mostly c. dat. (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴμοι</span>): c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἲ ἐμὲ δειλήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.408
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i> or Antip.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1971.5
			</span></i> : also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰοῖ, οἰοιοῖ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				177.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				841
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				876
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pers.</u>
				955
			</span></i> (all lyr.), etc. : 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀΐ</span> as exclam. of fear, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				933
			</span></i>.</div>
